FujiNet Go Odyssey 2 desktop -- milestone log and what is left

Status at v0.1.1 (see README.md "How this was verified" for the evidence).

DONE
  [x] M0  skeleton cloned from the Studio II desktop (v0.4.0); firmware pin =
          PR #2237's head (CONFIG 1154960, FujiNet logo) + the BoIP idle-wait
          fix (PR #2247, merged), fork branch tschak909/fujinet-firmware
          boip-idle-wait-on-o2-config (77d7dd3f3);
          runtime build script (anchors audited against the pin, libnfs
          strncpy patch, -Werror guard, Windows log-capture fix)
  [x] M1  8048 (mcs48.c) + disassembler (dasm48.c), traces identical to MAME on
          15 probes (147k instructions); all 256 opcodes' text identical
  [x] M2  8244/8245 (i8244.c): MAME scenes, beam, raster and sound replayed;
          157 real carts' register traffic replayed; debug snapshot/renderers
  [x] M3  FujiNet cartridge device (fujinet_cart.c) with reconnect; no-BIOS
          stand-in (stub.a48: vectors, readkey, getjoystick); cart mappers
          (standard, 4-in-1, rally, KTAA) by CRC
  [x] M4  session: machines, ROM import (file / zip / folder, own inflate),
          bindings, the 64-key matrix and two sticks, gamepads, media routing
  [x] M5  The Voice (SP0256, sample-exact vs MAME) and the Videopac+ G7400
          (EF9340/41, 8243, colour mixer; pixel-exact vs MAME on 12 scenarios)
  [x] M6  debugger engine (8048 + VDC + EF9340 + Voice views, breakpoints of
          every class, trace ring, FujiNet trace)
  [x] M7-M10  frontends: GNOME, KDE, Windows (D3D11), macOS -- see below
  [x] icons (case silver, inverted mark), accent (Odyssey red), COMPLIANCE.md

FRONTEND STATE
  KDE      built and run offscreen; QRhi GPU path and real-display behaviour
           of the fixed-size Controllers dialog unverified
  Windows  cross-built, run under Wine on a private Xvnc display; file dialogs,
           gamepads, audio, live FujiNet link and real D3D timing unverified
  GNOME    see the git log
  macOS    written against a Cocoa stub; first compile is on the GitHub runners

KNOWN GAPS / NEXT
  [ ] Atlantis' sprite multiplexing differs from MAME in ~0.3% of its pixels
      (CONFIG and most carts match; cause not found). First two power-on
      frames of every cart differ from MAME's.
  [ ] CONFIG on the FujiNet cart runs ONE FRAME AHEAD of MAME from frame ~9 on
      (our frames 3-9 differ, then the same pictures come a frame early). Seen
      at the splash -> hosts transition: our frames 159-165 are MAME's 160-166,
      pixel for pixel, six distinct frames. MAME is deterministic there (3
      runs). Not found: both cart models are synchronous, so look at the
      power-on beam phase. config_frames therefore samples steady pictures
      only (40/100/130 splash, 220+ hosts), never 159-165.
  [ ] config_boot and netboot tests (the real in-process FujiNet driving CONFIG
      and the firmware's fujiboot/fujitest clients) are parked: the sources
      still carry the Studio II calls (core/tests/config_boot_test.c,
      netboot_test.c); port them and re-enable in core/tests/CMakeLists.txt
  [ ] the Voice with real speech ROMs: the SP0256 core is sample-exact against
      MAME with the Intellivoice ROM, but the O2 Voice ROM layout ($4000 speech,
      $8000 a game's own) has never run against real data
  [ ] Chess (NSC800) and Home Computer (Z80) modules; C52 / Jopac / Odyssey 3
      machine rows
  [ ] the G7400's on-screen keyboard geometry is approximate (no photo)
  [ ] a public "this refusal is fixed by importing a ROM" accessor (the
      frontends match "Import BIOS" in the error text)
  [ ] fujinet-ads family banner (16 systems) and sibling README port tables
  [ ] when firmware PRs #2237 and #2247 merge: re-pin master, flatpak manifests
      back to `type: git`; the fork branch must not be deleted before that
